== a_pattern_on_numbers
note: 1 row with NA in day or level dropped (line 4)
error[Z0401]: `labels:` of `scale_x` as one string is the pattern an axis of dates is written by, and the `x` axis is one of numbers
 --> scripts/main.zeff:7:44
  |
7 | r.plot(x: level, y: level).scale_x(labels: "%Y")
  |                                            ^^^^ a pattern for dates
  |
  = help: for an axis of numbers, write a label for each break, as in `scale_x(breaks: [0, 1], labels: ["no", "yes"])`

== limits_in_numbers
note: 1 row with NA in day or level dropped (line 4)
error[Z0401]: `limits:` of `scale_x` on an axis of dates is a list of two dates, the first shown and the last
 --> scripts/main.zeff:7:19
  |
7 | p.scale_x(limits: [0, 1])
  |                   ^^^^^^ not two limits
  |
  = help: write the lower limit and the upper, as in `scale_x(date, limits: [date("2024-01-01"), date("2024-12-31")])`; `NA` in the place of one leaves that end to the dates drawn

== limits_the_wrong_way
note: 1 row with NA in day or level dropped (line 4)
error[Z0401]: the first limit of `scale_x` must be before the last, but they are 2024-12-31 and 2024-01-01
 --> scripts/main.zeff:7:25
  |
7 | p.scale_x(date, limits: [b, a])
  |                         ^^^^^^ not two limits
  |
  = help: write the lower limit and the upper, as in `scale_x(date, limits: [date("2024-01-01"), date("2024-12-31")])`; `NA` in the place of one leaves that end to the dates drawn

== one_limit
note: 1 row with NA in day or level dropped (line 4)
error[Z0401]: `limits:` of `scale_x` is a list of two dates, the lower limit and the upper, but this list has 1
 --> scripts/main.zeff:7:19
  |
7 | p.scale_x(limits: [a])
  |                   ^^^ not two limits
  |
  = help: write the lower limit and the upper, as in `scale_x(date, limits: [date("2024-01-01"), date("2024-12-31")])`; `NA` in the place of one leaves that end to the dates drawn

== breaks_in_numbers
note: 1 row with NA in day or level dropped (line 4)
error[Z0401]: `breaks:` of `scale_x` on an axis of dates is a list of dates, the values at which the axis has a tick, and each is a date
 --> scripts/main.zeff:7:19
  |
7 | p.scale_x(breaks: [1, 2])
  |                   ^^^^^^ not the breaks of an axis
  |
  = help: write the values at which the axis has a tick and a label, as in `scale_x(date, breaks: [date("2024-01-01"), date("2024-07-01")])`

== no_breaks
