 --> scripts/main.zeff:7:19
  |
7 | p.scale_x(breaks: [])
  |                   ^^ not the breaks of an axis
  |
  = help: write the values at which the axis has a tick and a label, as in `scale_x(date, breaks: [date("2024-01-01"), date("2024-07-01")])`

== a_directive_the_formats_lack
note: 1 row with NA in day or level dropped (line 4)
error[Z0401]: `labels:` of `scale_x` is the pattern the dates of the axis are written by, but `%Q` is not a directive of a date format
 --> scripts/main.zeff:7:19
  |
7 | p.scale_x(labels: "%Q")
  |                   ^^^^ not a pattern for dates
  |
  = help: a pattern is written as `format` writes a date: `%Y` the year, `%m` the month, `%d` the day, `%b` the name of the month, `%H:%M` the time, as in `labels: "%b %Y"`

== an_empty_pattern
note: 1 row with NA in day or level dropped (line 4)
error[Z0401]: `labels:` of `scale_x` is the pattern the dates of the axis are written by, but the format is empty
 --> scripts/main.zeff:7:19
  |
7 | p.scale_x(labels: "")
  |                   ^^ not a pattern for dates
  |
  = help: a pattern is written as `format` writes a date: `%Y` the year, `%m` the month, `%d` the day, `%b` the name of the month, `%H:%M` the time, as in `labels: "%b %Y"`

== a_pattern_that_ends_in_a_percent
note: 1 row with NA in day or level dropped (line 4)
error[Z0401]: `labels:` of `scale_x` is the pattern the dates of the axis are written by, but the format ends with a `%`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:7:19
  |
7 | p.scale_x(labels: "%Y %")
  |                   ^^^^^^ not a pattern for dates
  |
  = help: a pattern is written as `format` writes a date: `%Y` the year, `%m` the month, `%d` the day, `%b` the name of the month, `%H:%M` the time, as in `labels: "%b %Y"`

== labels_without_breaks
note: 1 row with NA in day or level dropped (line 4)
error[Z0401]: `labels:` of `scale_x` names the breaks one by one, so it needs `breaks:` to say where they are
 --> scripts/main.zeff:7:19
  |
7 | p.scale_x(labels: ["x"])
  |                   ^^^^^ not a label for each break
  |
  = help: write `breaks:` and a label for each of them, in the same order, as in `scale_x(breaks: [0, 1], labels: ["no", "yes"])`

== too_few_labels
note: 1 row with NA in day or level dropped (line 4)
error[Z0401]: `scale_x` has 2 breaks and 1 labels: each break has one label
 --> scripts/main.zeff:7:35
  |
7 | p.scale_x(breaks: [a, b], labels: ["x"])
  |                                   ^^^^^ not a label for each break
  |
  = help: write `breaks:` and a label for each of them, in the same order, as in `scale_x(breaks: [0, 1], labels: ["no", "yes"])`

== a_line_at_a_number
