== a_colour_for_one_line_at_a_date
note: 1 row with NA in day or level dropped (line 4)
error[Z0401]: `color:` of `vline` names the variable `site`, but `at:` is one date: there is one line, and no row to take its colour from
 --> scripts/main.zeff:7:23
  |
7 | p.vline(at: a, color: site)
  |             - one line
  |                       ^^^^ a colour for each row
  |
  = help: set one colour, as in `color: "firebrick"`, or draw a line for each row of a frame, as in `vline(data: means, at: wage, color: union)`

== a_line_at_a_date_with_no_axis
note: 1 row with NA in day or level dropped (line 4)
error[Z0401]: `vline` draws a line at a place on the `x` axis, but nothing is mapped to `x` yet
 --> scripts/main.zeff:7:18
  |
7 | r.plot(y: level).vline(at: a)
  |                  ^^^^^ needs an `x` axis
  |
  = help: map a variable to `x` where the plot starts, or add the layer that maps it before this one; a line at a place on the other axis is `hline`

== a_line_at_text
error[Z0401]: `at` of `vline` must be a Float, Date, DateTime or Var, but this is a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:7:13
  |
7 | p.vline(at: "2024-03-10")
  |             ^^^^^^^^^^^^ a Str
  |
  = help: usage: `p.vline(data: Frame, at: Float | Date | DateTime | Var, color: Var | Str, style: solid | dashed | dotted | dash_dot | long_dash | dash_dot_dot = dashed, width: Float = 0.5)`
